# Vite inlines this value into the JS bundle AT BUILD TIME — it is baked
# into the deployed static files, not read at runtime. Getting this wrong in
# a production build is a common cause of "login works, everything after
# 401s" or "calls the wrong backend" bugs, because rebuilding is the only way
# to change it afterward.
#
# Local development: leave this UNSET (or delete the line). The axios client
# falls back to the relative path '/api', which the Vite dev server proxies
# to the backend (see vite.config.js) — this makes the frontend and backend
# appear same-origin to the browser, which is the simplest and safest setup.
#
# Production, frontend and backend on the SAME origin (one Render service
# serving both, or a reverse proxy in front of both): also leave this UNSET,
# so requests go to the relative '/api' path on whatever origin actually
# served the page.
#
# Production, frontend and backend on DIFFERENT origins (e.g. a separate
# Render static site calling a *.onrender.com backend): set this to the
# actual deployed backend's origin + /api, e.g.:
#   VITE_API_URL=https://your-backend.onrender.com/api
# and set COOKIE_CROSS_SITE=true in the BACKEND's environment (see
# HRMS-server/.env.example) — a cross-origin deployment needs both changes
# together, not just this one.
#
# NEVER set this to a localhost URL for a production build — the browser
# loading the deployed site would try to reach the visitor's own machine, not
# your server.
VITE_API_URL=
